From ab30f2456a1763b9eadbd3257466e71f81bd50fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:20:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 41/55] power: supply: add explicitly armed J71t charging with
 rollback

Reconstruct D2365 input-current calibration and controls from the iOS
kernelcache. Require private CBAT, strict Tristar VBUS presence, safe
battery telemetry and an explicit 2400000-uA request for the owner-
verified Mac source. Program calibrated input and capped 2500-mA battery
limits while input is suspended; preserve unrelated bits and verify
every write. Restore handoff settings on disconnect, faults, suspend and
removal. No automatic source-current entitlement is inferred from VBUS.

Expose live ONLINE, input-limit and battery-current-limit readback. Use
the verified STOP-separated Tristar byte-read framing without writing IC
configuration or consuming interrupts. J172 policy is unchanged.

Validation: actual calibration and transaction functions pass 56
fault/guard cases under ASan/UBSan, including partial writes, mismatched
readback and rollback recovery. Hardware charging validation is pending.
---
